DOCKER COMMIT: docker commit creates a new image from the current state of a running (or stopped) container. It takes all the changes 
 that were made inside the container (files you added, packages you installed, config changes, etc.) and saves them as a new image layer.
 Basic syntax: docker commit [OPTIONS] CONTAINER [REPOSITORY[:TAG]]
Useful options
Option                      Meaning
-m "message"            Add a commit message (like a git commit) 
-a "Author Name"        Set the author
-c 'CMD ["..."]'        Change the default command of the new image
-p                      Pause the container while committing (default is true)
NOTE: This is not recommended because it has limitations


